SOLUTION 4 – Average Delivery Time by Route
Filter completed rows before applying the window function, ensuring non-completed deliveries do not affect the average.
SELECT
r.route_name,
d.driver_name,
x.delivery_time,
ROUND(
AVG(x.delivery_time) OVER (
PARTITION BY x.route_id
),
2
) AS avg_route_time
FROM Deliveries AS x
JOIN Routes AS r
ON x.route_id = r.route_id
JOIN Drivers AS d
ON x.driver_id = d.driver_id
WHERE x.status = 'Completed'
ORDER BY
r.route_name,
x.delivery_time,
d.driver_name;
Core ideas: JOIN supplies names; WHERE removes non-completed rows; AVG() OVER(PARTITION BY route_id) retains
each delivery row while calculating a route-level average; ROUND formats the average; ORDER BY matches the required
